WHY THIS CRATE IS GPL-3.0-only

LGPLv3 is, by its own opening sentence, the terms and conditions of version 3 of
the GNU General Public License supplemented by additional permissions. GPLv3
§7 ¶4 provides that when conveying a copy of a covered work "you may at your
option remove any additional permissions from that copy, or from any part of
it". Removing LGPLv3's additional permissions yields plain GPLv3, and that is
the option this crate exercises.

The v2.X-era LANL material is LGPL-2.1-or-later, so it may be taken at LGPL-3.0
and handled the same way; LGPL-2.1 §3 independently permits electing the
ordinary GPL. Battelle's supplementary permissive grant is one-way compatible
with GPL-3.0.

(An earlier revision of this file cited "LGPL-2.1 §3" as the route for the
upstream as a whole. LGPLv3 has no such clause — it was dropped as redundant
once GPLv3 §7 covered the case. The outcome was right; the citation was not.)

GPL-3.0-only is in any case the only option available to this crate, not merely
a permitted one: it links outram-foam-basic-lib, tampines-steam-tables and
outram-park-mpi, all GPL-3.0-only.

This is a provenance record, not legal advice.


PROVENANCE OF THIS CRATE'S OWN SOURCE — AUDIT OPEN (bead op-2nz)

src/ currently holds roughly 26,960 lines across 47 files. No file in it cites
an upstream PFLOTRAN .F90 source. Whether that code is independent work written
from the published theory and user manual, or is derived from upstream, has not
been established, and until it is this file makes no claim either way. An
earlier revision stated "No PFLOTRAN source has been ported into this crate yet
— it is a documented scaffold"; that statement cannot be reconciled with the
present contents of src/ and has been removed.

The reference clone vendored at upstream_source/PFLOTRAN (gitignored, never
committed) makes that comparison possible for the first time — it was not
reachable from the environment where the original record was written.

Where a Rust source file is found to be, or is written as, a translation of an
upstream routine, it must carry a provenance header naming the upstream source
file, version/commit, copyright holder and license, per the workspace
attribution rule.


